            "review_title": "Review at Babel Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Maryellen G\nVancouver, Canada84 contributions\n0\nExcellent food, nice atmosphere and decor!\nMay 2016 • Friends\nWe shared 6 dishes among 6 people: Prawns, Mango salad, salmon pasta, Hot Rock Beef (sizzling with beer, *Highly recommended--beef was tender and tasty), Frog, and Korean Hot Pot. Normally, I am not a big fan of hot pot, but the broth was spicy and flavorful. For dessert, the kitchen made us a durian/ginger smoothie, as a tasty end to the meal (palate cleanser!) All the dishes were delicious and I left with a satisfied belly. The restaurant is a bit hidden, but well worth the find. I would classify it as Western-Vietnamese fusion.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 7, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
