            "review_title": "Review at Babel Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Richard L\nHanoi, Vietnam6 contributions\n0\nHidden gem in Saigon\nJan 2016 • Business\nI am a traveling consultant and entrepreneur so I have been to many restaurants from michelin-starred to hidden local street food across the globe.\n\nThe restaurant has one the best view in town, you can see the entire skyline of Ho Chi Minh city from here. The restaurant is sitting on the 4 floor on a rooftop-like terrace of a high-end residential complex and the garden here is very impressive and well-design. I also saw a playground for kids, definitely bring my kids here next time.\n\nI had a beer, a beef \"sauna\" (quite interesting, the beef is steamed in a stone pot using beer), and a sea bass hot pot with local herb. The food is very well selected and not your typical local Vietnamese dishes!\n\nIt was early afternoon so I had the opportunity to chat with the head chef. Apparently he used to work at InterContinental hotel in downtown. Will definitely come back next time to try some pasta. Heard he came up with some interesting recipe.\n\nGreat find for me!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 30, 2016",
